{"availability":"available","full":"salsadsid/visualizer","name":"visualizer","description":"Step-by-step DSA visualizer for beginners: sorting algorithms with synced pseudocode and live variables, a Big-O playground and a 2D array visualizer. Next.js, no chart library.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":19,"forks":3,"created":"2024-09-18T11:53:43Z","updated":"2026-09-27T19:37:42Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://visualizer-gold.vercel.app","topics":["accessibility","algorithm-visualizer","algorithms","big-o","computer-science","data-structures","dsa","education","javascript","learn-to-code","nextjs","react","sorting-algorithms","sorting-visualizer","tailwindcss","visualization"],"demo":"https://visualizer-gold.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:27.452Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:27.452Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:27.452Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T00:25:38.763Z","stars":19,"forks":3},{"at":"2026-10-16T02:48:27.452Z","stars":19,"forks":3}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Press play, watch the bars move, follow the highlighted pseudocode and the live loop variables. Free, no sign-up, runs in your browser.","If this helps you learn or teach, a ⭐ helps other students find it."],"features":["One tiny step-trace engine, no chart or animation library. An algorithm is a plain function that records a list of snapshots. One usePlayer hook plays, pauses, steps and scrubs through that list, and shared components…","Pure by construction. The strict React Compiler lint rules are on (no setState in effects, no ref writes or impure calls during render), and CI runs lint, tests and a production build on every pull request.","Tested logic. The sorting engine, both input parsers and the page catalog are covered with node:test, with zero test dependencies.","Fast and accessible. Statically generated pages; Lighthouse (mobile